# Production Environment Variables
# This file is a template. Actual values will be injected via GitHub Secrets during deployment.
# 
# To setup:
# 1. Go to GitHub Repository Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions
# 2. Add the following secrets:
#    - VITE_API_URL: Your production API URL (e.g., http://your-api-domain.com or http://148.230.101.110)
#    - VITE_ABLY_KEY: Your Ably public key for real-time features
#    - SSH_HOST: Your server hostname/IP
#    - SSH_USER: SSH username
#    - SSH_PRIVATE_KEY: SSH private key for deployment
#
# For local production build testing, copy this file to .env and fill in the values

VITE_API_URL=your-production-api-url
VITE_ABLY_KEY=your-ably-key
